# 14. MODEL IMPROVEMENT LOOP

Implement the following lifecycle:

1. Coding agent receives user tasks.
2. Approved interactions are captured.
3. Sensitive information is removed.
4. Candidate examples are generated.
5. Teacher evaluates and corrects them.
6. Automated checks validate the examples.
7. Approved examples enter the dataset.
8. Dataset version is created.
9. Training scheduler checks whether enough new examples exist.
10. LoRA training job executes.
11. Candidate model is benchmarked.
12. Results are compared with production.
13. Model is promoted if it meets the required thresholds.
14. Previous model remains available for rollback.

Do not retrain continuously on every interaction.

Use configurable minimum dataset thresholds and scheduled batch training.

Implement human approval as the default requirement for major model promotions.

Provide an optional automated promotion mode with strict independent benchmark requirements.

